                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_08\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes the declaration of HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME in TetrisPanel.java from\n`private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";` to\n`private static final String HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";`.\nAssigning a String literal to an int-typed field is a compile-time type error in Java,\nmatching the fix commit message \"fix build error\".\n\ncandidate_08 is a large refactor of TetrisPanel.java that introduces this exact field for\nthe first time, declared with type `int` instead of `String`:\n`private static final int HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME = \"TetrisHighScores.txt\";`\nThe field is subsequently used as a filename string (e.g., `new File(HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME)`,\n`new FileWriter(HIGH_SCORES_FILENAME)`), confirming it was always meant to be a String and\nthat the `int` type was a mistake introduced in this commit's refactor of the constant\ndeclarations block (where WIDTH, HEIGHT, ROWS, COLUMNS, etc. were all converted to\n`static final` fields). No other candidate touches this declaration prior to the fix in\ncandidate_09, which is the fix commit itself.\n"
